{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G5fohQK8xgmF5vZA7V6bFM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and the review process:\n\n## Key Information:\n\n**Review Process:** EMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\n**Review Deadlines:** If you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:** All reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\n**Author Requirements:** ACL has adopted a policy similar to that of CVPR, requiring all authors to sign up as reviewers, with assignments made based on their qualifications. Reviewers who fail to fulfill their responsibilities may become ineligible to commit or (re-)submit papers in the following ARR cycle.\n\nThe specific reviewer form and detailed guidelines for EMNLP 2026 would be available through the OpenReview platform and the ACL Rolling Review website (aclrollingreview.org), which hosts the comprehensive reviewer guidelines for the ARR system that EMNLP 2026 uses.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"676cf70c-15aa-447c-a51d-1c9efb502147","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:56:13.173Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NtTuoFeUdYTTHC5TnusGoJ","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and the review process:\n\n## Key Information:\n\n**Review Process:** EMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\n**Review Deadlines:** If you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:** All reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\n**Author Requirements:** ACL has adopted a policy similar to that of CVPR, requiring all authors to sign up as reviewers, with assignments made based on their qualifications. Reviewers who fail to fulfill their responsibilities may become ineligible to commit or (re-)submit papers in the following ARR cycle.\n\nThe specific reviewer form and detailed guidelines for EMNLP 2026 would be available through the OpenReview platform and the ACL Rolling Review website (aclrollingreview.org), which hosts the comprehensive reviewer guidelines for the ARR system that EMNLP 2026 uses."],"durationSeconds":4.674552193000003}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wsz9uUtZ1wCCX6MycMQGvB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring rubric overall assessment scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"Decomposed Criteria-Based Evaluation of LLM Responses\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-industry.136.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Conference Decisions · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2023-statistics/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2025's review form scoring:\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5 point scale with half point increments, similar to ACL 2020. The detailed explanation for each point level is provided in the review form.\n\nThe Overall Recommendation section includes five subsections, covering reproducibility checklist, ethics review and justification, overall recommendation, reviewer confidence and best paper award recommendation and justification.\n\nFor reproducibility assessment specifically, scores of 1-5 are used to assess this aspect.\n\nThe search results indicate that the detailed rubric for what each specific score level means is available in the actual review form itself, rather than being fully specified in the publicly available reviewer instructions. For the complete scoring rubric with all descriptions for each point level, you would need to access the actual EMNLP 2025 review form directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"ffc7dc32-62a7-4048-9b45-068acad116a8","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:56:13.375Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring rubric overall assessment scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QTHwinNMHsh6HHHF4NTZGg","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"Decomposed Criteria-Based Evaluation of LLM Responses","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-industry.136.pdf"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf"},{"title":"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/"},{"title":"Conference Decisions · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"EMNLP 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2023-statistics/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2025's review form scoring:\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5 point scale with half point increments, similar to ACL 2020. The detailed explanation for each point level is provided in the review form.\n\nThe Overall Recommendation section includes five subsections, covering reproducibility checklist, ethics review and justification, overall recommendation, reviewer confidence and best paper award recommendation and justification.\n\nFor reproducibility assessment specifically, scores of 1-5 are used to assess this aspect.\n\nThe search results indicate that the detailed rubric for what each specific score level means is available in the actual review form itself, rather than being fully specified in the publicly available reviewer instructions. For the complete scoring rubric with all descriptions for each point level, you would need to access the actual EMNLP 2025 review form directly."],"durationSeconds":4.8395391450000025}}
