{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VgWDpftDMSFbDms6VjCJ4a","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment 1 2 3 4 5 scale criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/acl-rolling-review\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review assessment:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide specific details about a 1-5 scale rating system or detailed criteria for these assessments. The results indicate that excitement score is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper, and that soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review, and if you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation.\n\nTo get the specific criteria and scale information you're looking for, you may want to visit the official ACL Rolling Review Review Form page directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or consult the full ARR Reviewer Guidelines at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines, as those pages may contain more detailed rating scale criteria that weren't fully captured in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"9bb1fd03-a090-4f77-8530-d8bad404071f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:56:22.983Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment 1 2 3 4 5 scale criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LZcvxvfvvgSjjXPWAk56kv","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/acl-rolling-review"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review assessment:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide specific details about a 1-5 scale rating system or detailed criteria for these assessments. The results indicate that excitement score is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper, and that soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review, and if you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation.\n\nTo get the specific criteria and scale information you're looking for, you may want to visit the official ACL Rolling Review Review Form page directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or consult the full ARR Reviewer Guidelines at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines, as those pages may contain more detailed rating scale criteria that weren't fully captured in the search results."],"durationSeconds":5.2665084539999985}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UQ9Gv22KZgJp8JeNJpRUkD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness novelty\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results from aclrollingreview.org, I found relevant information about the review form's overall assessment and the evaluation criteria:\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of a paper and is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Soundness\n\nThe review form asks whether a paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, and whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them. The assessment includes different considerations depending on paper type:\n\nFor experimental papers: reviewers consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\nFor position papers and surveys: reviewers consider whether the current state of the field is adequately represented and main counter-arguments acknowledged.\n\nFor resource papers: reviewers consider the data collection methodology, resulting data, and the difference from existing resources described in sufficient detail.\n\n## Novelty\n\nThe Overall assessment score reflects assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact. Novelty is evaluated as part of the broader assessment process rather than as a separate score as of February 2025, when ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"20f204c5-d49e-41ec-bde1-ea0ceb6ec672","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:56:23.999Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness novelty","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016JkhjHNjHnqehzMHqpCosR","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"}]},"Based on the search results from aclrollingreview.org, I found relevant information about the review form's overall assessment and the evaluation criteria:\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of a paper and is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Soundness\n\nThe review form asks whether a paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, and whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them. The assessment includes different considerations depending on paper type:\n\nFor experimental papers: reviewers consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions investigated, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation.\n\nFor position papers and surveys: reviewers consider whether the current state of the field is adequately represented and main counter-arguments acknowledged.\n\nFor resource papers: reviewers consider the data collection methodology, resulting data, and the difference from existing resources described in sufficient detail.\n\n## Novelty\n\nThe Overall assessment score reflects assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact. Novelty is evaluated as part of the broader assessment process rather than as a separate score as of February 2025, when ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation."],"durationSeconds":6.075892049000002}}
