{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HBNC9jwo13bRtNh3XjN3k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:github.com acl-org aclrollingreview reviewform.md soundness excitement overall assessment score 1 2 3 4 5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewing.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewing.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/submissionform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/submissionform.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/authors.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/authors.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/actioneditorreviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/actioneditorreviewform.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/authors.md at master · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/master/authors.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewertutorial.md at master · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/master/reviewertutorial.md\"}]\n\nI found the information you were looking for. The search returned results from the ACL Rolling Review's review form documentation on GitHub.\n\nBased on the reviewform.md file from the ACL Rolling Review repository, here's what I found regarding the assessment scales:\n\n## Overall Assessment Score\n\nA score of 5 means \"Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\"\n\nA score of 2 means \"Resubmit next cycle: I think this paper needs substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle.\"\n\nA score of 1.5 means \"Resubmit after next cycle\" for papers needing substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle, while a score of 1 means \"Do not resubmit.\"\n\n## Soundness Evaluation\n\nFor Findings papers, the main criteria are soundness and reproducibility.\n\n## Excitement Scale\n\nThe form asks \"How exciting is this paper for you?\" noting that \"Excitement is subjective, and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\" A score of 5 on this scale means \"Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"b456fd18-86ae-414c-9013-f3fb95254304","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:56:40.540Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:github.com acl-org aclrollingreview reviewform.md soundness excitement overall assessment score 1 2 3 4 5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017jVyDzgK8ZxzgkqHcwkWVt","content":[{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewform.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewing.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewing.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/submissionform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/submissionform.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/authors.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/authors.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/actioneditorreviewform.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/actioneditorreviewform.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/authors.md at master · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/master/authors.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewertutorial.md at master · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/master/reviewertutorial.md"}]},"I found the information you were looking for. The search returned results from the ACL Rolling Review's review form documentation on GitHub.\n\nBased on the reviewform.md file from the ACL Rolling Review repository, here's what I found regarding the assessment scales:\n\n## Overall Assessment Score\n\nA score of 5 means \"Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\"\n\nA score of 2 means \"Resubmit next cycle: I think this paper needs substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle.\"\n\nA score of 1.5 means \"Resubmit after next cycle\" for papers needing substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle, while a score of 1 means \"Do not resubmit.\"\n\n## Soundness Evaluation\n\nFor Findings papers, the main criteria are soundness and reproducibility.\n\n## Excitement Scale\n\nThe form asks \"How exciting is this paper for you?\" noting that \"Excitement is subjective, and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\" A score of 5 on this scale means \"Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\""],"durationSeconds":6.356132262999999}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019gZwYyyLaT8Q1gcpszCFdo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough information about the EMNLP 2026 / ARR review form. Let me consolidate:\n\n**ARR Review Form (used by EMNLP 2026):**\n- Three main scores: Soundness, Excitement, Overall Assessment\n- Overall Assessment: 1-5 scale (with half-point increments)\n  - 5: Consider for Award (top 2.5%)\n  - 4-4.5: Strong accept / definite accept\n  - 3-3.5: Accept / borderline accept\n  - 2-2.5: Borderline reject / resubmit next cycle\n  - 1-1.5: Reject / do not resubmit\n- Soundness: 1-5 scale ranging from completely sound to fundamentally flawed\n- Excitement: 1-5 scale ranging from highly exciting to not exciting at all\n- Confidence: 1-5 scale\n\nGiven that EMNLP typically accepts around 20-25% of submissions, I need to set up two parallel reviewers—one focused on methods and experiments, another on novelty and related work. I'll have them work as agents simultaneously, then bring everything together for a roundtable discussion. Both reviewers need detailed, blind prompts with no tier information revealed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":58051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1197},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"27308cf0-c2e4-4284-bd71-3c4a8732df5a"}
