{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019gZwYyyLaT8Q1gcpszCFdo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MEt44HPbFSnzxSP94rba8J","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus areas are **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Venue: EMNLP 2026 (via ACL Rolling Review)\nScoring uses three dimensions:\n- **Soundness** (1-5): 5=completely sound, 4=mostly sound minor issues, 3=adequate with concerns, 2=significant issues, 1=fundamentally flawed\n- **Excitement** (1-5): 5=highly exciting, 4=exciting, 3=somewhat, 2=not exciting, 1=not at all\n- **Overall Assessment** (1-5, half-point increments): 5=award-worthy (top 2.5%), 4-4.5=strong accept, 3-3.5=accept/borderline accept, 2-2.5=borderline reject, 1-1.5=reject\n- **Confidence** (1-5): your expertise level\n- EMNLP acceptance rate ~22%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title:** \"Phase-Dependent Compound Sparsity Severity in Reasoning LLMs\"\n\n**Core claim:** Compound sparsity (attention head pruning + KV cache eviction) severity is phase-modulated: compound interaction amplifies monotonically across reasoning phases (paired median diff 0.39→8.48, Spearman ρ=1.0, n=500). Universal across 3 models, 2 architectures (Qwen2, LlamaForCausalLM), 2 math benchmarks (MATH-500, GSM8K). Strategy modulation is architecture-dependent (Qwen2 16.6× imp/rand ratio vs LLaMA 2.4×). Discrimination collapse (Gini/CV decline) identified as mechanism.\n\n**Three contributions:**\n1. Phase gradient universality — compound interaction severity increases monotonically from high→low sparsity reasoning phases, dz≈1.0-1.2 across all models, ρ=1.0\n2. Architecture-dependent strategy modulation — importance vs random eviction separation strong on Qwen2 (16.6×), weak on LLaMA (2.4×, 1/4 Bonferroni sig)\n3. Discrimination collapse mechanism — Gini/CV decline under head pruning, cross-model consistent\n\n**Methods (§3):**\n- Interaction Index (II): per-token metric = L_compound - (L_prune + L_evict - L_dense). Positive = super-additive.\n- Per-problem paired design: controls for problem-level confounds\n- Phase segmentation: quantile-based 3-way decomposition (high/mid/low sparsity) of dense model's attention sparsity\n- Phase gradient: Δ_i = median(II_low) - median(II_high), population-level paired median difference with bootstrap CIs (B=10000)\n- Stats: Wilcoxon signed-rank, Bonferroni correction (k=4), Cohen's dz paired, Spearman ρ dose-response\n\n**Experimental Setup (§3.5, §4):**\n- Models: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct (Qwen2 arch), DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B (LlamaForCausalLM)\n- All 7B/8B scale, bf16\n- Sparsity levels: s015, s020, s025, s030\n- Eviction strategies: importance-based, random\n- Benchmarks: MATH-500 (n=500 Qwen2, n=250 LLaMA), GSM8K (n=50), GPQA Diamond (n=50, appendix negative result)\n\n**Key Results:**\n- Table 1: MATH-500 DS median diff 0.391→8.481, QW 0.066→3.155, both ρ=1.0, all Bonferroni p<0.005\n- Table 2: LLaMA importance dz=0.97-1.12 at all levels, all Bonf sig, ρ=1.0\n- Table 3: Strategy specificity — Qwen2 DS 16.6×, QW 3.5×, LLaMA 2.4× (1/4 Bonf sig)\n- Table 4: LLaMA imp-rand dz=0.09-0.21, only s030 Bonf sig\n- GSM8K: DS 0.241→4.682, QW 0.039→2.092, both ρ=1.0\n- GPQA: 0/10 significant, non-monotonic with direction reversals\n- Discrimination collapse: Gini/CV decline cross-model consistent, entropy inconsistent\n- Pilot mitigation: 18% recovery (p=0.002) below pre-registered 30% gate\n\n**Experiment design reference (what was planned):**\nThe full experiment plan included 5 imagined experiments:\n1. LLaMA n=250 cross-architecture validation (8 conditions: importance/random × 4 sparsity) — INCLUDED in paper\n2. GPQA DeepSeek importance sweep (4 sparsity levels, n=50) — INCLUDED as appendix negative result\n3. GPQA Qwen importance sweep (4 sparsity levels, n=50) — INCLUDED as appendix\n4. GPQA random masking controls (DS s025+s030) — INCLUDED as appendix\n5. GPQA cross-task synthesis — INCLUDED as Table 5\n\nAll 5 planned experiments appear to be covered in the paper. The LLaMA experiment has n=244 valid (vs planned 250).\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nWrite a detailed review focusing on:\n\n### A. Methods Evaluation\n1. Is the Interaction Index (II) well-defined and appropriate? Any issues with the formulation?\n2. Is quantile-based phase segmentation principled or ad hoc? Does it actually capture meaningful reasoning stages?\n3. Is the statistical framework appropriate (Wilcoxon, Bonferroni, bootstrap)?\n4. Are there confounds the paired design does NOT control for?\n5. Is the \"discrimination collapse\" mechanism sufficiently validated or just correlational?\n\n### B. Experiments Evaluation\n1. Are the experimental conditions comprehensive enough? Missing conditions?\n2. Is n=500 / n=250 / n=50 adequate for the claims made?\n3. Is the head pruning ratio p fixed or varied? (Note: paper mentions p but never specifies its value!)\n4. Are baselines/comparisons adequate? What's missing?\n5. How well do GPQA results support/undermine the claims?\n6. Is the pilot mitigation study adequate (n=50, pre-registered gate not met)?\n7. Any concerns about reproducibility?\n\n### C. Detailed Scoring\nProvide scores with justification for: Soundness, Excitement, Overall Assessment, Confidence.\n\n### D. Summary\n- 3 strengths (bullet points)\n- 3+ weaknesses (bullet points)  \n- Questions for authors (numbered)\n- Missing experiments or analyses\n\nWrite your review in full detail. Be rigorous but fair."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1197,"cache_read_input_tokens":58051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1197},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f803c3f7-d0f1-4587-9cc5-4b6689d0c433","uuid":"1896169f-1625-418d-b334-38ea5ba69e4a"}
